==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}}, from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|tribut}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|tributum||tribute, literally 'a thing contributed or paid'}}, neuter of {{term|tributus}}, past participle of {{term|tribuere||to assign, allot, grant, give, bestow, etc.}}, usually derived, from {{term|tribus||tribe}}; see [[tribe]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-tribute.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[acknowledgment]] of [[gratitude]], [[respect]] or [[admiration]]; an [[accompanying]] [[gift]].
#: ''Please accept this as a '''tribute''' of our thanks.''
# A [[payment]] made by one [[nation]] to another in [[submission]].
# [[extortion|Extortion]]; [[protection money]].
# A payment made by a [[feudal]] [[vassal]] to his [[lord]].

====Related terms====
* [[tribe]]
* [[tribal]]

